*passwd*.txt
secrets
secrets.txt
*secret*.txt
*secret*.json
*secret*.yml
*secret*.yaml
# "secretary" contains "secret": the patterns above must not swallow project
# source (this bit the initial commit — 4 of 5 roles landed). Directory-scoped
# un-ignores beat a basename exception: they also cover future role variants
# (secretary_v2.yml) and fixtures. detect-secrets guards actual key material.
!config/modes/*.yml
!tests/fixtures/*.json
client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
*credential*.txt
# Case-insensitive variants: git patterns are case-sensitive on Linux, and a
# real "Slack Credentials ... .txt" note with a capital C reached a commit
# before these lines existed (amended out before any push).
*[Cc]redential*
*[Tt]okens*
*[Tt]oken\ *
*\ [Tt]oken*
service-account*.json
# Scoped to credential-like extensions (2026-09-02): the previous bare
# catch-alls also swallowed reviewed source/docs ABOUT keys, e.g.
# docs/api-keys-and-scopes.md or src/llm/apikey_rotation.py.
*[Aa][Pp][Ii]?[Kk][Ee][Yy]*.txt
*[Aa][Pp][Ii]?[Kk][Ee][Yy]*.json
*[Aa][Pp][Ii]?[Kk][Ee][Yy]*.yml
*[Aa][Pp][Ii]?[Kk][Ee][Yy]*.yaml
*[Aa][Pp][Ii]?[Kk][Ee][Yy]*.csv
*[Aa][Pp][Ii][Kk][Ee][Yy]*.txt
*[Aa][Pp][Ii][Kk][Ee][Yy]*.json
*[Aa][Pp][Ii][Kk][Ee][Yy]*.yml
*[Aa][Pp][Ii][Kk][Ee][Yy]*.yaml
*[Aa][Pp][Ii][Kk][Ee][Yy]*.csv
*.token
